Title: ...consisting of all of them...
Status: draft

Keep in mind that most of the existing user community is deploying mod_apreq2 in a middle-tiered cluster behind HTTPS gateway(s), so the statistics reported by <https://webtechsurvey.com/technology/mod_apreq2> represent only a fraction of the total deployed user base.

Yet, flash forward to 2026, and you can see public adoption is on the upswing again, despite Apache's best effort to kill apreq in its crib.

